  partName: Bottom Gasket
  description: The Bottom Gasket is a tiny, thin-flat component located at the bottom-center-front
    of the engine, made of Material.006, which plays a crucial role in sealing the
    engine block to prevent oil and coolant leaks. Its position and material ensure
    a tight seal, and an interesting detail is that it must be replaced if damaged
    to maintain engine performance. The Bottom Gasket's small size belies its importance
    in overall engine reliability.
  audioExplanation: {fileID: 0}
